===Etymology===
{{rfe|en|What is the evidence for direct inheritance from Old English instead of two separate borrowings from Latin?}}

From {{inh|en|ang|India}}, {{m|ang|Indea}}, from {{der|en|la|India}}, from {{der|en|grc|Ἰνδία}}, from {{der|en|grc|Ἰνδός|t=Indus river}}, from {{der|en|peo|𐏃𐎡𐎯𐎢𐏁|tr=hi<sup>n</sup>dūš}}, from {{der|en|sa|सिन्धु}}, ultimately from {{der|en|iir-pro|*síndʰuš|t=river}}.

Compare {{cog|enm|Inde}} and {{m|enm|Ynde}} from {{cog|fro|Ynde}} (original form started to prevail in the 16th century), {{cog|fa-cls|هند|tr=hind|t=India}}, {{cog|sa|सिन्धु|tr=síndhu|t=a river, stream}}.

